WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.400
Legislative Timeline.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:17.100
From the Carter v. Canada Supreme Court ruling in 2015, through Bill C-14 legalizing MAID in 2016, to Bill C-7's expansion in 2021 removing the requirement that death be reasonably foreseeable.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:28.637
Mental illness expansion has been delayed twice, now pushed to 2027 after opposition from psychiatrists, disability organizations, and UN human rights bodies.
